{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>And they said to him.</b> Rashi's comment: there is a dot over the alef-yod-vav. And wherever the letters outnumber the dots, you interpret the letters. And if you ask: why did they not place dots over the lamed alone, so that the letters would outnumber the dots and be interpreted? — unless it would have been implied, apparently, that they first asked Sarah, 'Where is Abraham?' and afterward asked Abraham, 'Where is Sarah?' — which is not so, for they saw Abraham first, whereas Sarah they did not see until the time of eating. But now that alef-yod-vav is dotted, it indicates that 'אליו' does not belong here, i.e., they asked Abraham, 'Where is Sarah?' and then asked Sarah, 'Where is Abraham?' And so Rashi explained regarding 'הנסתרות' (the hidden things), which is dotted to indicate that it does not belong there."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {0 "The comment quotes Rashi's interpretation of the dotted letters in אליו; the argument about dotting the lamed alone assumes that four undotted letters against one dot would yield the written form 'אליו' for interpretation, whereas the actual Masoretic tradition dots all three letters alef-yod-vav."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:40.139012432Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}